<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harari</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Harari are a Semitic-speaking Muslim people of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harar">Harar</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. They were closely associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a>. Harari contingents fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> forces in the coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Imam Ahmad</a> ibn Ibrahim against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>.</p></div>
